{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The outdoor Gorilla tape feels like a natural choice because I have bought Gorilla tape before, and weather resistance gives it a clear purpose for exposed repairs.",
    "The steel-reinforced epoxy fits my interest in practical repair materials while offering a way to make rigid repairs that tape or vinyl cement might not handle."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Cutting wheels, wood screws and long bolts require particular tools, materials or dimensions; my repair purchases do not establish a need for those specific jobs.",
    "Oil and electronic cleaner could be useful someday, but I have no current lubrication or contact-cleaning task. Likewise, sealant and leak putty are relevant only when I have a matching repair."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My purchases seem to have been taken as a broad interest in almost any workshop or maintenance supply, although I choose supplies for particular tasks.",
    "Buying hose clamps and wire connectors seems to have been taken as a reason to offer other plumbing and electrical products, even though those purchases do not establish a leak or dirty electrical contacts."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated Gorilla tape purchases provide a clearer reason to choose a related tape than my occasional purchases provide for unrelated repair supplies.",
    "Something can fit my repair habits without being worth buying now: I would choose the outdoor tape over another bulk tape supply and wait for a specific need before buying sealant or putty."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my practical repair interests, but often stretch them into specific maintenance needs that my purchases do not establish."
}"}
